  "answer": "The playbook lists the Enterprise onboarding target timeline as 8–10 weeks [NL-031-S02] and similarly describes Enterprise Plan Onboarding as 8–10 weeks [NL-005-S02]. The observed Enterprise average is 8.7 weeks [NL-012-S06], which also matches the Q2 segment average validation of 8.7 weeks [NL-031-S03]. So the observed Enterprise average falls within the playbook range.\n\nEnterprise onboarding is longer than simpler plans because it requires security reviews, custom data-processing agreements, nested Active Directory/Okta permission sync configurations, custom data-retention policies, SSO setup, and OCR processing of scanned legacy documents [NL-005-S02][NL-031-S02]. These steps are driven by compliance and file-format complexity, not present in Starter or Growth plans, which typically involve clean, public-facing documents, no complex RBAC, and simpler permission setups [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02]. Enterprise delays are also commonly caused by permission mapping, SSO/security review, and scanned PDF cleanup/OCR [NL-015-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
